From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:28:43 -0400
Subject: welcome: a first-run flow in place of the bare search-engine chooser

chrome://stedding-welcome, floating over a profile's first window as a
child window of it: choose the search engine (the chooser Stedding already
required, through the same service, or the same choice-screen data where
Chromium has no chooser), import bookmarks, history and passwords from
another browser (Chromium's ImportDataHandler), pick light or dark, make
Stedding the default browser, and read the five shortcuts worth knowing.
Every step is skippable; stedding.welcome.shown records that it ran, and
--no-first-run suppresses it. Not a window-modal sheet: Chromium refuses to
quit while the active window has one. docs/features/welcome.md W1-W6.

Why: the first minute decides whether a switcher stays; the bare chooser
was a legal notice, not a welcome.

Removable when: never; this is product behaviour.
